Now the STREAM frame serializer: it should write the offset/length according to the frame type flags rather than inferring from nullability. Let me look at the StreamFrame parser/serializer again:

StreamFrameSerializer:
```java
writeFrameType();
writeStreamId();
if (frame.getOffset() != null) writeOffset();
if (frame.getLength() != null) writeLength();
writeData();
```

Per the contract ("Do not infer flags from nullable DTO fields", "Lengthless frames stay lengthless"), the serializer should follow the frame type: if the type has the OFF flag → write the offset; if it has the LEN flag → write the length.

Let me fix that.

Also the DataBlockedFrameSerializer, StreamsBlockedFrameSerializer etc. are fine.

